If you don't wish to recompile anything you can open the nethack
executable that uses compress and find & edit the string manually to
read /usr/bin/gzip instead of /usr/bin/compress . Replace the remaining
letters with \0 (NUL) characters. Then open the other one and replace
all ".gz" to ".Z\0" (i.e. again padding with \0). That will get rid of
the compress problem; the script becomes simpler:
--
#!/bin/sh
echo Choose mode:; cd; ls .nethackrc.* | sed "s/^.nethackrc./- /" ;
echo -n "> "; read s;



FILE=$HOME/.nethackrc.$s
NETHACKOPTIONS=@$FILE `head -n 1 $FILE | sed "s/^#!//"`
--
Now name your options files .nethackrc.q, .nethackrc.t, etc. and include
a #!/path/to/nethackversion in the top line of these.

